{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nRebar has measured mutation evidence for seven behavioral cores, but Gerrit does not detect\nwhen a changed test weakens those contracts. Mutmut changes production code, so changed tests\nmust select the production shard they cover. The blocking lane stays targeted; a weekly/manual\nall-shard sweep detects mapping and tool drift.\n\n## Approach\n\nUse the targeted, pinned pattern seen in active OSS workflows, adapted to rebar's Gerrit\n`Verified` authority. `.github/mutation-shards.toml` is the sole source for each\nshard's production selector, test/support inputs, normalized equivalent-mutant fingerprints,\nand numeric budgets. The driver generates the effective per-shard mutmut configuration and a\nhuman-readable summary from that manifest; `pyproject.toml` and the documentation do not carry\nindependent shard lists or budget values.\n\nThe driver diffs the commit against its single parent, including both sides of renames. A mapped\nsource, test, or support change selects its shard;\nmutation driver/config/lock changes select all shards. Changed files under `tests/` that match no\nprotected shard are reported as advisory mapping gaps. An unresolved parent/diff fails closed;\nan empty selection is a successful, explicit skip.\n\nEach shard runs from fresh base/head archives with no restored `mutants/` verdict state.\nDependency caching is allowed. Python 3.12, `mutmut==3.7.0`,\n`--max-children 1`, mutmut's `(clean-test duration + 1 second) x 15` timeout, and a 30-minute job\nlimit bound the run. Selected clean tests run before mutation.\n\nComparison is per mutation unit (module + qualified function). When its source bytes are\nidentical at base and head, every base killed mutant must still exist and be killed at head; this\nalso applies to unchanged functions in mixed source+test patches. Changed units use head budgets\nbecause valid edits can add or renumber mutants; exact-ID deltas are advisory. A survivor is\naccepted only when the normalized `mutmut show` diff\n(location headers removed) matches a manifest fingerprint and the shard remains within its\nsurvivor ceiling. Zero mutants, unknown statuses/fingerprints, or budget failures block.\n\nAllowed head outcomes are killed mutants, fingerprinted equivalent survivors within budget,\nand `no tests` results within their separate historical ceiling. Timeout ceilings are zero.\n`not checked`, interrupted, suspicious, skipped, segfault, caught-by-type-check, and unknown\nstatuses fail because this gate does not enable type-check filtering and cannot prove those\nmutants were exercised. Mapped score is `killed / (killed + survived + timeout)`.\n\nOn failure, head non-killed mutants rerun once to classify regressions versus nondeterminism;\neither stays red. Only independently identified dependency-install/setup\nfailures may retry. Results and raw outputs are always published, and newer patchsets cancel\nolder runs.\n\nThe Gerrit implementation is explicit: `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` invokes a targeted\n`mutation` job on the exact patchset and lists it in `vote.needs`.\n`.github/workflows/test.yml` has the push/PR mirror job required by the source-lane parity contract\nat `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py:44-58`; the broad workflow reuses the driver and manifest.\nThis matches vote aggregation at `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:310-317`.\n\nHistorical ceilings from `docs/mutation-testing.md:98-120` are:\n\n| Shard | Survivors max | No-tests max | Timeouts max | Score floor |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| signing | 3 | 110 | 0 | 99.2% |\n| reducer processors | 5 | 0 | 0 | 99.4% |\n| next batch | 6 | 208 | 0 | 99.2% |\n| gates | 0 | 376 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| validate | 0 | 223 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| compact policy | 0 | 0 | 0 | 100.0% |\n| push policy | 0 | 0 | 0 | 100.0% |\n\nA budget may change only with the affected source or mapping, measured base/head results, and\nan updated rationale. A budget-only relaxation fails validation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/mutation-shards.toml`, `scripts/mutation_gate.py`: canonical shard data, selection,\n  clean base/head execution, comparison, fingerprints, and failure classification.\n- `.github/workflows/_mutation.yml`, `.github/workflows/mutation.yml`: reusable targeted runner\n  and weekly/manual all-shard sweep.\n- `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, `.github/workflows/test.yml`: exact-patchset Gerrit job,\n  `vote.needs`, and its push/PR mirror counterpart.\n- `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`: pin mutmut 3.7.0 and remove the duplicate global shard selection;\n  the driver writes effective per-shard config into each fresh archive.\n- `docs/mutation-testing.md`: explain cadence, manifest authority, fingerprint/no-tests rationale,\n  unmatched tests, and budget-change policy without duplicating manifest values.\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`: hermetic driver\n  behavior and workflow/vote parity.\n\n## Testing\n\nHermetic tests cover selection including renames/deletions, unmatched tests, manifest validation,\nmixed patches, statuses, fingerprints, budgets, failures, reruns, artifacts, and vote aggregation.\nA real mutmut 3.7.0 smoke run executes compact-policy from fresh base/head archives.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Selection tests prove mapped source/test/support and infrastructure changes choose the\n  specified shards, unmatched tests are advisory, empty selection is explicit, and unresolved\n  parent/diff fails closed.\n- [ ] Fresh-archive tests prove base/head runs restore no mutation verdict cache, use the pinned\n  runtime/concurrency/timeouts, run clean tests first, and reject zero parsed mutants.\n- [ ] Comparison tests prove identical mutation units block missing or killed-to-non-killed base\n  mutants, including unchanged functions in mixed patches.\n- [ ] Changed-unit tests prove exact-ID deltas are advisory while unknown statuses/fingerprints or\n  survivor/no-tests/timeout/score budget failures block.\n- [ ] Failure-policy tests prove only setup may retry, mutation reruns remain red, and output\n  distinguishes skip/mapping gap, baseline test, setup/tool, timeout, regression, and nondeterminism.\n- [ ] Workflow tests prove the targeted job exists in Gerrit and the push/PR mirror, appears in\n  `vote.needs`, cancels stale patchsets, always publishes artifacts, and passes\n  `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py`.\n- [ ] A weekly/manual all-shard workflow uses the same manifest, driver, budgets, and artifacts as\n  the targeted job.\n- [ ] A real compact-policy smoke run with mutmut 3.7.0 passes from fresh base/head archives.\n- [ ] Documentation names the manifest as authoritative and explains cadence, fingerprints,\n  no-tests allowances, mapping gaps, and the measured budget-change rule.\n\n## Verification\n\n    pytest -q tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py\n    python scripts/mutation_gate.py smoke --shard compact-policy --base HEAD^ --head HEAD\n    python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py\n    make lint\n    make typecheck\n\n## Primary evidence\n\n- Mutmut 3.7.0: https://github.com/boxed/mutmut/blob/3.7.0/README.rst\n- Instructor: https://github.com/567-labs/instructor/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation.yml\n- DataDog: https://github.com/DataDog/dd-license-attribution/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation-regression.yml\n- PostHog: https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-python/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n- Trailmark: https://github.com/trailofbits/trailmark/blob/main/.github/workflows/mutation.yml\n- GeoParquet: https://github.com/geoparquet/geoparquet-io/blob/main/.github/workflows/nightly.yml"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786421310910913001,"uuid":"c68e44a1-2652-4309-9cba-fc7d4e2346df"}